<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Bolognese Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1796 CE – 1796 CE · capital Bologna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The brief republic set up in Bologna in 1796 after the French expelled papal rule, which soon merged into the Cispadane Republic.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In June 1796 French troops entered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-bologna">Bologna</a>, part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States</a>, and the papal legate left. The city's Senate, under French protection, took over the government, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a> declared itself a free republic.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna's</a> old ruling families kept much of their influence, governing through the Senate and new committees while meeting French demands for money and art. The republic drafted a constitution in late 1796. It sent delegates to the congresses that united <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-bologna">Bologna</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reggio-emilia">Reggio</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By the end of 1796 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-bologna">Bologna</a> had joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cispadane-republic">Cispadane Republic</a>, which in 1797 became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cisalpine-republic">Cisalpine Republic</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1796 CE – 1796 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.44%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1796 CE – 1796 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bologna</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian, Emilian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Italy</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Bologna (1796)</dd></dl></aside></div>
